<article class="env-lemma" id="0EBS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EBS">Lemma <span data-tag="0EBS">41.14.3</span>.</a> Let $U \to X$ be an étale morphism of schemes where $X$ is a scheme in characteristic $p$. Then the relative Frobenius $F_{U/X} : U \to U \times _{X, F_ X} X$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The morphism $F_{U/X}$ is a universal homeomorphism by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CCB" data-tag="0CCB">33.36.6</a>. The morphism $F_{U/X}$ is étale as a morphism between schemes étale over $X$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GW" data-tag="02GW">29.37.19</a>). Hence $F_{U/X}$ is an isomorphism by Theorem <a href="/tag/025G" data-tag="025G">41.14.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>